course: dictionary
lesson: 9269
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one is meant. The word sow is a good example. Look at the words around it before you decide.
explain: «A farmer sows the grain, and the plants grow all spring.» Here sow means to plant seeds in the ground. Check by putting plant in its place: the sentence still makes sense, so this is the right meaning.
explain: «A sow, a mother pig, can have a litter of a dozen piglets.» Here sow is a noun, a name for a female pig. The clues are mother pig and piglets. Listen to the sound too: when sow means a pig, it rhymes with cow.
explain: Sow can also mean to cause something to start or spread. «You reap what you sow» is a saying that means what you do comes back to you later. The meaning is not about seeds at all, so the context makes it clear.
fact: Sow has several meanings, so always check the context to find the right one.
fact: «Sow» as a verb, rhyming with go, means to plant seeds in the ground.
fact: «Sow» as a verb can also mean to cause something to start or spread, as in sow doubt.
fact: «Sow» as a noun, rhyming with cow, means an adult female pig.
fact: Phrases such as sow the seeds of and reap what you sow use the word in a special way, so learn them as whole groups of words.
exercise: «A farmer sows the grain in spring.» What does sows mean here? | *To plant seeds in the ground | To cut the stalks in summer | To swim across a river | To cook a meal
exercise: «A sow usually has about 8 to 12 piglets.» What kind of animal is a sow? | A type of plant | A bird | A farmer's dog | *A female pig
exercise: «The farm girl sows carrot seeds in May.» Find and copy the word that means to plant seeds. | May | *sows | carrot | seeds
test: «The bully tried to sow doubt among the team.» What does sow mean here? | To sing loudly | An adult female pig | *To cause something to start or spread | To plant seeds in the ground
test: «You reap what you sow» is a saying. What does it mean? | You will get a big harvest if you plant a lot | Pigs eat a lot of grain | Farmers are always busy in spring | *What you do comes back to you later
exam: «The sow fed her piglets in the barn.» What does sow mean in this sentence? | A small green plant | *An adult female pig | To cause something to spread | To plant seeds in the ground
